From c5db27ff3ee3784f75c132c1881a26dfbaff85db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:45:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix item-sales SQL bug, add period filter to Dues/Dealers,
 chart export
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- get_team_member_item_sales: "order by qty" was ambiguous between the
  output alias and items.qty, throwing live on every call. Order by the
  aggregate expression instead. This also restores the item-wise sales
  export buttons, which were gated on data that never loaded.
- Dues and Dealers drill-downs get their own period pill (defaults to
  "All time", matching today's behaviour): picking a period narrows the
  list to dealers with order activity in that window, since outstanding
  itself is a running total with no date of its own.
- Every report's PDF/Excel button now opens a sheet to pick which
  representations go into the file (Number table / Bar graph / Pie
  chart, or all three). PDF renders the chosen chart(s) as extra pages
  drawn straight into jsPDF (rect bars, triangle-fan pie wedges) — no
  screenshot library needed. Excel stays number-only, since a
  spreadsheet cell can't hold a chart image the same way.
- PDF exports now use fmtCurrencyPdf (Rs.) instead of fmtCurrency (₹)
  for money columns — jsPDF's built-in fonts don't have the ₹ glyph and
  were silently substituting a stray "1", matching the convention the
  rest of the app's PDF exports already follow.

